import P2qJumps.P7Kernel.K7
import P2qJumps.P7Kernel.K8
import P2qJumps.P7Kernel.K9

/-!
# P2qJumps.P7Kernel

Kernel certificates (`decide +kernel`, no `native_decide`) that the checker `desc` of
`P2qJumps.P7Defs` returns `true` for `ω(N) = 7, 8, 9`: `P7Cert.cert7`, `P7Cert.cert8`,
`P7Cert.cert9`. Wherever a subtree of the descent has more than 100 nodes, the certificate is split
over the next prime `r` prime to `210` (`P2qJumps.P7Kernel.Lemmas`), and large subtrees are put in
their own modules `P2qJumps.P7Kernel.K*`, so each kernel evaluation stays small. The modules are
generated by `scripts/p7/gen_kernel.py`; the generator is not trusted.
-/
